  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 325°F. Coat a 9 x 13-inch baking dish with cooking spray. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 spritz nonstick cooking spray"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, and roughly chop mushrooms. Place in a large bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ lb white mushrooms"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, wash, dry, trim, and seed bell pepper; small dice. Add to the bowl with the mushrooms.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 red bell pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add veggies and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and cooking liquid has evaporated, 6-8 minutes. Remove from heat. (Reserve bowl for the next step.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n¾ tsp Italian seasoning\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, place eggs, milk, salt, and pepper in the reserved bowl. Whisk to combine, then pour into the baking dish. Sprinkle sautéed veggies evenly over egg mixture.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp whole milk\n¾ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking dish in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and bake until eggs are set in the center, 18-22 minutes. Remove from oven and set aside to cool completely, about 1 hour. (The eggs will continue to firm up as they cool.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the eggs are cool, cut into 12 squares.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Split English muffins in half. Top half with a veggie-egg square and slice of cheese, then close sandwiches with remaining halves.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "12 slice smoked Gouda cheese, sliced"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "STORING: Wrap each sandwich in parchment paper, then transfer to a storage container or resealable bag and place in the freezer for up to 1 month. \n\nREHEATING: For best results, thaw sandwich(es) in the fridge overnight. Remove parchment from the sandwich and heat in a microwave or toaster oven until cheese is melted and sandwich is warmed through. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
